-- title:
--   Branch tangent lines on the Drinfeld chart descend along ψ
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $W_0$ and $W$ be commutative local rings and $\psi \colon W_0 \to W$ a ring homomorphism. Assume the maximal ideal of $W_0$ is the principal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, and that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and in that of $W$. Let $f_0, u_0, v_0$ be power series in $W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ (formal power series in the two variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$) with $u_0$ a unit and $f_0 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, the Drinfeld form being $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$. Let $Q$ be a prime ideal of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ such that: the coefficientwise image under $\psi$ of $\pi_0 v_0 - f_0 u_0$ lies in $Q$; at least one of $X_0$, $X_1$ does not lie in $Q$; the constant $\psi(\pi_0)$ lies in $Q$. Suppose further that for some integers $a$, $b$ there is $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2 \subseteq W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $aX_0 + bX_1 + h \in Q$. Then the same linear form is realised by a correction term coming from $W_0$: there exists $h_0 \in (X_0,X_1)^2 \subseteq W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ whose image, together with that of $aX_0 + bX_1$, satisfies $\psi_*(aX_0 + bX_1 + h_0) \in Q$.
--
--   The statement says that a prime of the base-changed Drinfeld chart lying over $\pi_0$ and having tangent line $aX_0+bX_1$ with integral coefficients already has that tangent line witnessed by a power series with coefficients in $W_0$, so that the tangent line of such a branch prime is unchanged by the base change $\psi$. It is used in the analysis of the completed stalks of the Drinfeld chart on the full-level modular curve, where branch primes over the cyclotomic coefficient ring must be compared with branch primes over a general coefficient ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_exists_mem_sq_map_add_mem_of_linearPart_mem_of_isPrime.lean

